e Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:12:34-07:00","id":1394036,"title":"","content":"I made it a long time ago, probably unbalanced af but <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1o5kL_Sk4EVxBedX0OtOKs-twE4ZcTClT2RQJDN3vvZU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a> There it is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T08:52:06-07:00","id":1394052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SamuraiMujuru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1394028#post1394028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Toad style is immensely strong and immune to nearly any weapon. When it's properly used it's almost invincible!<br /> <br /> Did they settle on calling it Poison Toad? I know Vance said it's directly inspired by 5 Deadly Venoms, which would mean less poison and more offensive iron body.<br /> <br /> One step closer to my Venom Mob circle... just need Scorpion and Lizard. (Tough there's a really damn good fan made Scorpion)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't know what the names of the styles are. Names are based on what I do know about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T09:12:18-07:00","id":1394055,"title":"","content":"Toad, Monkey, Bear, Rat and Thousand Blades are the official names. Toad is tough and poisonous, Monkey is Sun Wukong-inspired, Bear is brutal and grapply, Rat is sneaky and disease-spreading, and Thousand Blades is an esoteric First Age Martial Art that mortals cannot practice and which lets Sublime Danger achieve her Daiklave Wings look. That's about all I remember said about the styles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T11:36:07-07:00","id":1394099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1393972#post1393972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monkey because this time round the wheel it's inspired by Sun Wukong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It always was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T15:22:07-07:00","id":1394164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1394099#post1394099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It always was.</div> </div> </div> </div>But not in the best way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T16:55:50-07:00","id":1394184,"title":"","content":"I wasn't aware it was. Mostly it didn't feel that way to me, this time around I'm hoping it will. The wrackstaff as a weapon out the gate and a more mischievious and destructive style. Course that's just my opinion on how it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T17:12:26-07:00","id":1394186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1394184#post1394184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't aware it was. Mostly it didn't feel that way to me, this time around I'm hoping it will. The wrackstaff as a weapon out the gate and a more mischievious and destructive style. Course that's just my opinion on how it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree. I also think that if there's any MA style that should have a shadow clone charm, it should be Monkey. All the gate stuff and the mini DBT were IMO very meh...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T19:17:37-07:00","id":1394213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1394186#post1394186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I agree. I also think that if there's any MA style that should have a shadow clone charm, it should be Monkey. All the gate stuff and the mini DBT were IMO very meh...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know, Lunars have that in their own charmset already, so if it\u2019s a Lunar geared Style (based on what book it\u2019s in) I\u2019d rather it not be something that\u2019s great for non-Lunars to be more like Lunars, while being redundant for Lunars.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m just hoping it\u2019s an evasion heavy, acrobatic misdirection style. That would be particularly appealing to Lunars I think because their own Charms favor soak over dodge for defense as heavily as they do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-05-2020, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-04T23:36:54-07:00","id":1394265,"title":"","content":"I can see not having that redundancy if the style was created by a lunar. Not sure I buy into the styles being geared for lunars though, anymore than i see the three non elemental dragon styles being geared specifically for DB's. I don't think being named after an animal, or inspired by a lunar like real world myth makes it geared for lunars unless they are going to key of things like the toemic and protean keywords. Snake, tiger, and falcon don't, and falcon is from the lunar book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T00:07:47-07:00","id":1394269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arkayriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1394265#post1394265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see not having that redundancy if the style was created by a lunar. Not sure I buy into the styles being geared for lunars though, anymore than i see the three non elemental dragon styles being geared specifically for DB's. I don't think being named after an animal, or inspired by a lunar like real world myth makes it geared for lunars unless they are going to key of things like the toemic and protean keywords. Snake, tiger, and falcon don't, and falcon is from the lunar book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Falcon is absolutely geared to Lunars as they\u2019re the ones best positioned to get use out of it via flight. There are other ways to use it, and non-Lunars can invest in ways to get access to flight, but Lunars by far have the easiest access to make the widest use of the style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T01:12:34-07:00","id":1394279,"title":"","content":"Flying does make for no brainer setups (do they suffer the atacking while flying penalty I wonder?), but it's hardly required to go aerial, solars and deebs both having aerial launching floaty style charms.And what about Laughing Monster, Centipede and Swaying Grass Dance style? They're in the lunar book as well and how are they geared towards lunars over others? I should've been clearer, I don't see the styles in the lunar book as lunar geared, nor do I believe the news styles will be either. It's fine if you do though, it's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T02:05:23-07:00","id":1394287,"title":"","content":"To further clarify, I feel that to be geared towards a particular exalt type you have to have charms that work off a feature exclusive to that type. An example would be the aura keyword from the deebs. The dragon styles can only be fully utilised by them so they are geared towards them. The Falcon style is best utilised in an aerial manner that can be accessed without flight. Furthermore any character can, through some difficulty, gain access to flight. Flight itself is not limited to lunars. The fact that the Falcon style is aerial is to mimic that animal in the same way Tiger style mimics a tiger. Not so that it's a style primarily for lunars. The only thing about those charms that is dependent on exalt type is the mastery and terrestial key words. One could then say that all styles with those keywords are geared towards solars and geared away from deebs, but I wouldn't as those are more intrinsinc features of the exalt types and not something that was engineered into those styles. The dragon styles have no mastery keyword and were designed by sidereals to be specifically for the dragon blooded. I hope this makes my point clear even if you or others disagree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24445,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","user":"Arkayriel","date":". 06-05-2020, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T03:27:58-07:00","id":1394292,"title":"","content":"Uh...apologies glamourweaver, I somehow failed to correct in my second post an acknowledgement of your statement that others could gain flying. My apologies, I wasn't deliberately ignoring that, I just don't feel flying is all that necessary to make excellent use of the style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24445-arkayriel","name":"Arkayriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T09:25:07-07:00","id":1394372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1394186#post1394186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I also think that if there's any MA style that should have a shadow clone charm, it should be Monkey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though there are limits to how far the Sun Wukong inspiration can go while it still feels like a Martial Art native to the setting and emulating its named animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:02:24-07:00","id":1394381,"title":"","content":"Also, some of Sun Wukong's powers are already present in the Lunar charmset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T10:02:37-07:00","id":1394382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1393940-martial-arts-in-many-faced-strangers?p=1394186#post1394186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I agree. I also think that if there's any MA style that should have a shadow clone charm, it should be Monkey. All the gate stuff and the mini DBT were IMO very meh...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I mean except the Lunar Charm set has the shadow clone shennigans. I'm...a bit at a lost at what Sun Wukong's influence would be, I feel like Laughing Monster and Lunar charms have him fairly covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby